  "items": [
    {
      "name": "What's actually causing the pain",
      "char_file": "근육경련_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Right before an egg",
        "is released, the growing",
        "follicle stretches the",
        "surface of the ovary",
        "",
        "Fluid released when it",
        "ruptures then irritates",
        "the lining of your",
        "abdomen — prostaglandins",
        "drive both steps"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "It's more common than you'd think",
      "char_file": "달력_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "More than 40% of women",
        "of reproductive age",
        "get this at some point —",
        "and for many, it shows",
        "up almost every cycle",
        "",
        "It's usually felt on",
        "one side only and lasts",
        "anywhere from a few",
        "minutes to about 48 hours"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Start with heat",
      "char_file": "온찜질_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "A heating pad or hot",
        "water bottle on your",
        "lower belly relaxes",
        "the muscles",
        "",
        "and takes the edge",
        "off the ache fast"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "NSAIDs work well too",
      "char_file": "이부프로펜_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Taking ibuprofen at the",
        "first sign of pain blocks",
        "the same prostaglandins",
        "that are causing it",
        "",
        "It's one of the most",
        "reliable ways to take",
        "the edge off"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Track your cycle so you're not caught off guard",
      "char_file": "달력_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Mark the days you expect",
        "ovulation on a calendar",
        "or period-tracking app",
        "",
        "so you can keep meds",
        "on hand before the",
        "pain even starts"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "When it's not just ovulation pain",
      "char_file": "근육경련_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "See a doctor if the pain",
        "lasts more than 48 hours,",
        "or comes with nausea,",
        "vomiting, or dizziness",
        "",
        "Sudden, severe one-sided",
        "pain needs urgent care —",
        "it could be ovarian",
        "torsion or a ruptured cyst"
      ]
    }
  ],
